# File Naming & Organization Conventions

## Directory Structure Standards

### Root Level Organization
```
rolet-mix/
├── src/                 # Source code
├── public/              # Static assets
├── .cursor/             # Cursor IDE rules and settings
├── components.json      # shadcn/ui configuration
├── next.config.ts       # Next.js configuration
├── tailwind.config.ts   # Tailwind CSS configuration
├── package.json         # Dependencies and scripts
└── tsconfig.json        # TypeScript configuration
```

### Source Code Organization (`src/`)
```
src/
├── app/                 # Next.js App Router pages
│   ├── layout.tsx       # Root layout
│   ├── page.tsx         # Homepage
│   ├── globals.css      # Global styles
│   └── favicon.ico      # Favicon
├── components/          # React components
│   ├── ui/              # Reusable UI primitives
│   ├── layout/          # Layout components
│   ├── sections/        # Page sections
│   └── [feature]/       # Feature-specific components
└── lib/                 # Utilities and libraries
    └── utils.ts         # Utility functions
```

### Public Assets Organization (`public/`)
```
public/
├── images/              # Static images (logos, icons)
├── videos/              # Video files
├── animations/          # Animation files (Lottie, etc.)
├── logo-light.svg       # Brand assets at root level
└── *.svg                # Other shared SVG icons
```

## File Naming Conventions

### Component Files
- **Format**: PascalCase with `.tsx` extension
- **Examples**: 
  - `HeroSection.tsx`
  - `MagicButton.tsx` 
  - `FullscreenMenu.tsx`
  - `TextGenerateEffect.tsx`

### Page Files (App Router)
- **Format**: lowercase with `.tsx` extension
- **Examples**:
  - `page.tsx` (homepage)
  - `layout.tsx` (layout)
  - `loading.tsx` (loading UI)
  - `error.tsx` (error UI)
  - `not-found.tsx` (404 page)

### Configuration Files
- **Format**: kebab-case with appropriate extension
- **Examples**:
  - `next.config.ts`
  - `tailwind.config.ts`
  - `components.json`
  - `eslint.config.mjs`
  - `postcss.config.mjs`

### Utility and Library Files
- **Format**: camelCase with `.ts` extension
- **Examples**:
  - `utils.ts`
  - `constants.ts`
  - `helpers.ts`
  - `api.ts`

### Asset Files
- **Images**: kebab-case with descriptive names
  - `logo-light.svg`
  - `hero-background.jpg`
  - `product-showcase.png`
- **Videos**: kebab-case with context in parentheses
  - `hero-background (light).mp4`
  - `product-demo (mobile).mp4`

## Component Organization Patterns

### UI Components (`src/components/ui/`)
Single-purpose, reusable components:
```
ui/
├── AuroraBackground.tsx     # Visual effect component
├── LogoGenerateEffect.tsx   # Animation component
├── MagicButton.tsx          # Interactive button
├── MenuTrigger.tsx          # Menu control
└── TextGenerateEffect.tsx   # Text animation
```

### Layout Components (`src/components/layout/`)
Structural and navigation components:
```
layout/
├── Navbar.tsx              # Main navigation
├── FullscreenMenu.tsx      # Mobile/overlay menu
├── Footer.tsx              # Site footer
└── Sidebar.tsx             # Side navigation
```

### Section Components (`src/components/sections/`)
Page-specific content sections:
```
sections/
├── HeroSection.tsx         # Homepage hero
├── AboutSection.tsx        # About content
├── ServicesSection.tsx     # Services showcase
├── PortfolioSection.tsx    # Work examples
└── ContactSection.tsx      # Contact form
```

### Feature-Specific Components
Group related components by feature:
```
components/
├── auth/
│   ├── LoginForm.tsx
│   ├── SignupForm.tsx
│   └── PasswordReset.tsx
├── products/
│   ├── ProductCard.tsx
│   ├── ProductGrid.tsx
│   └── ProductFilter.tsx
└── admin/
    ├── Dashboard.tsx
    ├── UserManagement.tsx
    └── Analytics.tsx
```

## Import Path Conventions

### Alias Configuration (from [components.json](mdc:components.json))
```typescript
"aliases": {
  "components": "@/components",
  "utils": "@/lib/utils", 
  "ui": "@/components/ui",
  "lib": "@/lib",
  "hooks": "@/hooks"
}
```

### Import Examples
```typescript
// Components
import HeroSection from "@/components/sections/HeroSection";
import MagicButton from "@/components/ui/MagicButton";
import Navbar from "@/components/layout/Navbar";

// Utilities
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// Hooks (when created)
import { useLocalStorage } from "@/hooks/useLocalStorage";
```

## Special File Conventions

### Next.js App Router Special Files
- `layout.tsx` - Defines UI shared across routes
- `page.tsx` - Creates route segments
- `loading.tsx` - Loading UI for segments
- `error.tsx` - Error UI for segments
- `not-found.tsx` - 404 UI for segments
- `route.ts` - API route handlers

### Component Export Patterns
```typescript
// Default export for main component
const HeroSection = () => {
  return <section>Content</section>;
};

export default HeroSection;

// Named exports for utilities or multiple components
export { Button, ButtonGroup } from "./Button";
export const utils = { helper1, helper2 };
```

## Code Organization Within Files

### Component File Structure
```typescript
"use client"; // Client directive if needed

// 1. External imports
import React, { useState, useRef } from "react";
import { motion } from "framer-motion";
import { FiArrowRight } from "react-icons/fi";

// 2. Internal imports
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
import MagicButton from "@/components/ui/MagicButton";

// 3. Types and interfaces
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  className?: string;
}

// 4. Constants and variants (outside component)
const containerVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  visible: { opacity: 1 }
};

// 5. Main component
const Component = ({ title, className }: ComponentProps) => {
  // Hooks
  const [state, setState] = useState(false);
  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  
  // Event handlers
  const handleClick = () => {
    setState(!state);
  };
  
  // Render
  return (
    <div className={cn("base-styles", className)}>
      {title}
    </div>
  );
};

// 6. Default export
export default Component;
```

## Asset Organization Guidelines

### Image Optimization
- Use WebP format for photos when possible
- Use SVG for icons and simple graphics
- Organize by context: `images/logos/`, `images/products/`, etc.

### Video Organization
- Keep videos in `public/videos/` 
- Use descriptive names with context
- Consider multiple formats for compatibility

### Icon Management
- Prefer SVG icons in `public/` for static icons
- Use Lucide React for interactive icons
- Use React Icons for brand/social icons